    "excerpt": "AI systems now have higher penetration in the enterprise than a year ago and are now moving from experimental tools to decision-making agents. As a result, the question of AI safety is rapidly shifting from a research concern to a practical necessity. In enterprise settings, AI systems don’t just generate text or recommendations; they initiate actions that modify databases, trigger workflows and affect real users. Failures in these environments can be catastrophic for the enterprise. A single incorrect action can cascade across interconnected systems, violating business constraints or creating compliance and security risks. AI safety in the enterprise is fundamentally about ensuring reliable behavior under complexity, partial information, and long-horizon consequences.",
